   "reason": "Port to Zig 0.17.0."
  },
  {
   "path": "examples/3_3D/main.zig",
   "original_sha256": "2d0e6a0ac8ad5f2ce8ede48cccad2de608641e4a8cb2789a5014b9ee753c9b3c",
   "current_sha256": "bec0a7e714a067febaf8242c8a4a725b5d26f870740466126c4ba7492964453c",
   "reason": "Use the drawIndexed interface that reads index format from the buffer. Port to Zig 0.17.0."
  },
  {
   "path": "examples/5_indirect_triangles/main.zig",
   "original_sha256": "c5b13d32b6d3446733166c0633d89023d8809db19c1893fd58a9cf570648420d",
   "current_sha256": "9d1a8d3638fb0e8bbc8c840671328d456d1afc11085e095efdf7043536960d05",
   "reason": "Use the drawIndexedIndirectMulti interface that reads index format from the buffer. Port to Zig 0.17.0."
  },
  {
   "path": "examples/7_deferred_async_load/main.zig",
   "original_sha256": "4d5cbc7f652957d000dd94b4e2c898fadd55cc26fa7ba3d8b89eedf03bd4b3b5",
   "current_sha256": "17f6dc5899c99749bb6cf8c20220d950a755e11ad4022c8ff6c075f1a086e8cb",
   "reason": "Port to Zig 0.17.0. Load the newly authored shaders/sky.ppm asset instead of the image with unknown provenance."
  },
  {
   "path": "examples/common.zig",
   "original_sha256": "2008f3c02e37a28c27c8527fc007ae48c7f7cc835e7415f225a074a9e4c1f7b2",
   "current_sha256": "424d42f0e49439aa6d7352874007be5623b73d5075873dd9b34eb9b41569450e",
   "reason": "Create native surfaces through Surface.initSdl, with one owner and no raw Vulkan handles in example callers."
  },
  {
   "path": "noapi/CommandBuffer.zig",
   "original_sha256": "587297c23be3db03ba9d5ade6e7091ef2fa1ec877e62662581bec6129e009a06",
   "current_sha256": "30dea7bdd5a27a10858371f3167c824cb71ead59180b1e53db641a6e399e200c",
   "reason": "Add the pixel_scale push constant that carries physical framebuffer pixels per logical window unit, and document screen as the logical window size. Port to Zig 0.17.0."
  },
  {
   "path": "noapi/Gpu.zig",
   "original_sha256": "75a1615e1b1e4425f3570b8a8e6b519ba90d51736df2ae0b440d3080488105ca",
   "current_sha256": "25fde373e81636f469f3c2ef8933724ba3fe261f80e7d554adac5771ec2ae4b4",
   "reason": "Add commandsCancel to discard an unsent offscreen command buffer, and reject a cancelled buffer handle in copyCommandBufferHandles. Port to Zig 0.17.0."
  },
  {
   "path": "noapi/Queue.zig",
   "original_sha256": "1f9f6916f680b64af3bdba125c5358384760d301d608494ca498bbe73309685d",
   "current_sha256": "c3c681061d8e30bd7308f1f34fa65b894121eb93346f1ce481fb6e8bc337318c",
   "reason": "Reject a cancelled command buffer in copyCommandBufferHandles so an aborted offscreen frame cannot enter timeline submission. Port to Zig 0.17.0."
  },
  {
   "path": "noapi/Shader.zig",
   "original_sha256": "c84af8e5a88ce43040ce296ec6e6c0dacc518688166c51b69022f4c434e93dbb",
   "current_sha256": "f44e98924c686e2b70c04f822efdf8b901bfacadc6736ccc525eb9b54c84743d",
   "reason": "Port to Zig 0.17.0."
  },
  {
   "path": "noapi/Surface.zig",
   "original_sha256": "6b0b0497da4b41d9a40c787a27e197ad5168feae7fb864f2ad7881531a3f13b8",
   "current_sha256": "a554012b1572558d7bbec9a15338e10acd67ce6c1af3ce4df0c7fd4a914fae7e",
   "reason": "Add abortFrame to discard active recording. Make initSdl the sole public surface factory, using an SDL-compatible callback without exposing Vulkan handles. Release the platform surface exactly once if adoption fails. Port to Zig 0.17.0."
  },
  {
   "path": "noapi/vk.zig",
   "original_sha256": "ba8d3189013562be364a156e9d8e805b42f5bd17db6bc2f45c67ca7f6fa6d9c8",
   "current_sha256": "27bc37954bb22d9a6ec315c3e72e208f9ffeca5874ea243fa95fb43f801b72e4",
   "reason": "Port to Zig 0.17.0."
  },
  {
   "path": "noapi/VkBackend.zig",
   "original_sha256": "9e069e1b82e04a87d4d24ac3ad5aac1d390a0b294da47333c68fd8e8eb339d5f",
   "current_sha256": "40c9c4559f3a97f31104bc476d79e9ccb183ae2569b3224a1cd93c28013dfe8f",
   "reason": "Track per-window frame recording state and add abortFrame and commandsCancel, so an unfinished frame or an unsent offscreen command buffer is discarded instead of resubmitted and a duplicate frame call fails with FrameAlreadyActive or SurfaceFrameUnrecoverable; mirror pixel_scale in the graphics push constants with comptime layout asserts, keep command buffer ownership with the caller when submission fails, report software rasterizers through GpuInfo.software_emulation, and release partial window resources on failed surface adoption while leaving platform-surface ownership with the caller; include draw_indirect_bit alongside indirect_command_read_bit for draw_arguments hazards; report swapchain_recreated only after an actual rebuild, re-arm suboptimal acquisition, and keep every changed pixel extent pending without a two-frame resize throttle; log the bounded device-name slice rather than its zero-padded Vulkan property buffer. Additionally: cached image views are now deferred into the same pending_free drain that protects their image, instead of being destroyed eagerly while the descriptor still names them. Port to Zig 0.17.0."
  },
  {
   "path": "test/main.zig",
   "original_sha256": "a0ff738a3cb20d26f9e48bb9a9d6418f12bcb37d609c8060c725a206792eadad",
   "current_sha256": "e1c897ca30ad15e5b6dbc872eeb5539ff2d33032ea9d57e74e1b03ce9a59d8c8",
   "reason": "Use drawIndexed with buffer-owned index format and migrate every native surface creation to Surface.initSdl. Port to Zig 0.17.0."
  }
 ],
